12. Mini Challenge (Try Without Looking at the Solution)

Create a component that displays:

Student Name: Ravi

Age: 21

Course: React Development

College: ABC Engineering College

Requirements:

Use variables for all values.
Render them using JSX.
Wrap everything inside a single parent element.

Spend 10–15 minutes trying it yourself before checking the solution.

13. Solution
function App() {
  const studentName = "Ravi";
  const age = 21;
  const course = "React Development";
  const college = "ABC Engineering College";

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Student Name: {studentName}</h1>
      <p>Age: {age}</p>
      <p>Course: {course}</p>
      <p>College: {college}</p>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
Line-by-Line
const studentName = "Ravi"; → Creates a variable for the student's name.
const age = 21; → Stores the age.
const course = "React Development"; → Stores the course name.
const college = "ABC Engineering College"; → Stores the college name.
return (...) → Tells React what to display.
{studentName}, {age}, {course}, {college} → JSX evaluates these JavaScript variables and inserts their values into the UI.
14. Summary
Rendering means displaying or updating the UI.
React renders components into the browser.
React updates only the changed parts of the page.
JSX uses {} to embed JavaScript expressions.
A component must return a single parent element (or a React Fragment <>...</>).
React uses the Virtual DOM and Reconciliation to update the UI efficiently.
15. Exam Notes
Rendering: Converting React components into visible UI.
Virtual DOM: Lightweight copy of the real DOM.
Reconciliation: Comparing old and new Virtual DOM trees.
JSX Expressions: Use {} to insert JavaScript values.
Single Root Rule: Wrap sibling elements in one parent or a Fragment.
16. Revision Flashcards

Q: What is rendering?
A: The process of displaying or updating the UI.

Q: What does the Virtual DOM do?
A: It helps React detect changes efficiently before updating the real DOM.

Q: What is Reconciliation?
A: React's process of comparing Virtual DOM trees and updating only the changed parts.

Q: How do you display a JavaScript variable in JSX?
A: Use curly braces: {variable}.

Q: Can a component return multiple sibling elements directly?
A: No. They must be wrapped in one parent element or a Fragment.

