18. Industry Tips
Keep components focused on a single responsibility to make rendering easier to understand and optimize.
Avoid unnecessary re-renders by updating only the state that actually changes.
Use descriptive variable names (employeeName instead of x) for readability.
Use React Developer Tools in your browser to inspect components and understand when they render.
When debugging rendering issues, add console.log("Component rendered") inside a component to see when React renders it.
